From: Proton CRM <noreply@proton.local>
Subject: [PATCH] P7 task 3: agent-facing translate action

Gives an agent reading a Malay, Tamil, or Chinese customer message a one-
click way to read it in English: a small "Translate" button in the reply
composer's top panel (next to the existing Copilot button) that calls
POST /assist/translate for the latest customer message. Backs
translate_router.py.

WHY THIS DOES NOT INSERT TEXT ANYWHERE. The three existing Proton actions in
this same file (reply_suggestion/summarize/ask_copilot, patch 0002) each
return a string the panel inserts into the reply box or note composer.
Translate is different on purpose: translate_router.py posts the translation
directly into the conversation as a private note (never an outgoing message
-- see that file's module docstring for the customer-safety invariant), so
there is nothing for this panel to insert. This action therefore stays a
separate method (handleTranslateLastCustomerMessage) rather than being added
to the PROTON_ACTIONS/PROTON_ACTION_MODE maps above, which both assume a
reply/note string exists to route somewhere. On success the button shows a
toast confirmation; the private note itself appears via Chatwoot's own
realtime conversation update, the same way any other private note does.

Visibility is gated on `protonEnabled` (the same ai_assist feature surface
0002 already reads) -- a client-side convenience only, not the real
boundary. The actual gates are the backend's own: `translation_enabled`
(returns {disabled: true} and does nothing when off, so a stale/cached
frontend build cannot bypass it) and the `translation.use` RBAC permission
via require_permission (granted to the default "agent" role). A tenant with
translation_enabled=False sees this button do nothing but show "Translation
is not enabled on this account."

The outbound-Tamil split (translation_outbound_tamil_enabled) still holds:
the backend refuses target "ta" with a 403 while that flag is off, and the
button surfaces that as "Translating into Tamil is not enabled yet."

FIX-21 (2026-11-09) LANGUAGE PICKER. Clicking Translate now opens a row of
four choices -- English, Bahasa Malaysia, 中文, தமிழ் (codes en/ms/zh/ta, the
backend's allow-list; anything else is a 400). Picking one translates the
composer draft into that language when there is draft text, otherwise the
customer's last message (English is the first choice, so the usual read-in-
English flow is one click away). The note header now reads the real target
("en → ms"), not a hard-coded "en". Edited additions-only where possible:
the handler signature, the `protonEnabled` guard line and the button/`</div>`
skeleton that 0056 and 0074 use as context are unchanged; the picker row is
appended at the end of the template.

